title: FirstLoopFabianParade
tags:
---

Amongst the hustle and bustle of the parade preparations, you see Fabian standing around holding something in his hands. 
He’s looking here and there, as if trying to find somewhere he can help, but ending up stuck in paralysis. 
Once you approach him, he notices you and stops his constant turning.
<< if $FabianMood lte -2 >> //Unhappy
	A faint smile forms in his face. He seems unsure first of whether to address you or not
	Fabian: I’m glad to see that you came, Sasha. Have you talked to your brother yet?
<< elif $FabianMood gte 2>> //Happy
	A cheerful smile opens on his face. He attempts to wave at you with his hand only unsuccessfully.
	Fabian: Sasha! Just who I wanted to see!
<< else >> //Perfectly neutral
	He greets you with a nod and a smile.
	Fabian: Sasha! I’d give a wave, but my hands are currently occupied.
<< endif >>
Now that you are closer to him, you can see the object in his hands is an urn.
It is painted with the appearance of a priest, wearing a similar attire to Alfonz himself, a black priest’s garb with a small symbol of a star on the lapel.
The drawn figure is lacking a face. Despite this, it is quite familiar to you.

-> ”What are you holding?”
    Sasha: ”What are you holding?”
    You know his answer already before his mouth opens.
	Fabian: It’s the urn.
	Fabian: Alfonz’s urn.
-> ”Is that his…?”
    Sasha: ”Is that his…?”
	You know his answer already before his mouth opens.
	Fabian: Yes. It’s Alfonz.

<< if $FabianMood lte -2 >> //Unhappy
	His faint smile fades. He looks into your eyes for a moment, then averts his gaze.
<< elif $FabianMood gte 2>> //Happy
	His cheerful smile fades. He looks into your eyes for a moment, then averts his gaze.
<< else >> //Perfectly neutral
	His smile fades. He looks into your eyes for a moment, then averts his gaze.
<< endif >>

<< if $PsychMajor == true >>
	Avoiding eye contact, a sign of shame, a feeling that you have done something wrong.
	Does he feel that he is intruding in your reunion with Alfonz? 
    Or perhaps is he ashamed that this is the best reunion he can provide for you with your old friend?
    His shoulders shrink, he makes himself small. A feeling of inadequacy, powerlessness. It’s the latter.
    It's only now that you realise that you misjudged.
    You are projecting. It is you who is feeling small. So, so small.
    You stomach twists. Your breathing is tense, and fast, and faster, and faster.
    Act normal. You know how to act normal. You studied this. This is what you know. Focus.
    You wipe your eyes, and steady your nerves. You'll be okay. 
<< elseif $ArtMajor == true >>
	It is an odd sort of reunion. Instead of Alfonz, you are greeting this painted mimicry of him. 
    In the details you can see subtle changes to him in the years you were away. 
    His hands gained more wrinkles. His garb gained more creases. The most crucial part is left to your imagination.
    You try filling in that detail. From the recesses of your memory, you project Alfonz's face onto the blank canvas.
    His friendly, smiling face, looking into your eyes.
    His smiling face that you have not seen in years.
    His face that you will never see again.
    His face that you have been denied a final chance to glimpse.
    His crying, twisting face... No, no, he didn't cry. He's not the one crying.
    Fabian says nothing, and gives you some needed space.
    Your sleeve is a little wetter now. But you are okay. It's just a wooden urn.
<< elseif $TechMajor == true >>
	The urn is handcrafted. You can see flaws in the woodwork that a factory build would lack. Some stone seems to be worked into it too, to allow it to sink.
	The painting of the urns is done by those close to the defunct, so it makes sense that their construction would be too.
	why does the urn look so shabby? Why are the edges so sharp, why is the varnish so sloppy?
    Did they not care? Did they not care at all about the vessel where your dead, gone friend would be laid to rest?
    He doesn't deserve this. He deserves so, so much more. He deserves the best, most perfect urn that he could have gotten.
    He didn't deserve any of this. He didn't deserve to die. He didn't need to die. Not before you could ever meet him again.
    Not before you could have met him again, seen him again, saw how he looked now so you could make him the best urn in the whole damn world.
    You feel your heart beating fast. Indignation flows through your veins. 
    You need to channel this feeling into something, do something with it, you have to. You feel like exploding, like blowing up, like destroying something.
    You need... You need to calm down. You focus your breathing, slower, and slower. This is no time for anger.
    You wipe your eyes and steady yourself. You are in control again. You'll be okay.
<< endif >>

<< jump FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1 >>

===

title: FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1
---

<< declare $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Ashes = false >>
<< declare $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Face = false >>

-> “Is there anything inside? Since there can’t be any ashes...” << if $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Ashes == false >>
    Sasha: “Is there anything inside? Since there can’t be any ashes...”
	Fabian: There is. When we have no ashes to put in an urn, we put a star token inside to represent them.
	Stars are one of the main symbols of the Solster faith. 
    It’s a strange tradition, given you never saw a real night sky star until you left Solster.
	Fabian: One of the members of his congregation made it with clay. A girl who cared quite strongly about him. Said he was like a father to her.
	Fabian: I wish you could have seen it before we sealed the urn. It was quite beautiful.
	You feel the weight of four years of history that you missed in his words. 
    You are far from the last person Alfonz made an impact on…
    << set $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Ashes = true >>
    << jump FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1 >>
-> “Why does it have no face?” << if $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Face == false >>
    Sasha: “Why does it have no face?”
	Fabian: Oh, right. The face…
	He seems hesitant to answer your question. In the end, he continues.
	Fabian: It was your brother’s idea. He thought you’d like to be the one to paint his face onto the urn.
	Fabian: We did think that you’d arrive a little sooner.
	Fabian: But it was just an unfortunate miscommunication. There is nobody to blame here.
	He adds that second part hurriedly, maybe realising that he does not want to make you feel guilty about it.
	It doesn’t really work. Alfonz is going to be sent off faceless, muted, and blind, and it is your fault.
    Don't go into a self-loathing spiral. Stay steady for now. You'll have all the time to hate yourself after this Parade is over.
	Fabian: On the topic of your brother… Did you find him? I haven’t seen him around yet, though I only just got here.
	
	<< if DoesHeKnow ("DmitriyTarot") >>
		<<jump SeenDmitriyParadeTime>>
	<<else>>
		-> "No.."
			Sasha: "No.."
			He looks a little surprised- not so shocking considering all that was expected of you to do over the last couple of minutes was find this man.
			Fabiam: Ah, well that's all right. I'm sure he's around here somewhere- speak to him first, and then we can talk about the parade.
			He's not firm about it, but he's clearly not interested in continuing the conversation.
		-> "Yes, I did."
			Sasha: "Yes, I did."
			Fabian: Oh, really?"
			His eyes widen, but there's a moment of hesitation that follows soon after. He's not sure if he believes you.. maybe you looked too smug after that [i]Yes[/i]-noise.
			Fabian: Well.. uh..
			He clears his throat, then stands straighter.
			Fabian: How about you come ask him to join us and watch the parade? I'm sure his break is over by now.
			He's trying to be polite- almost too obviously so- but you can't get away with your poor lying in this situation.
	<<endif>>
	
===
title: SeenDmitriyParadeTime
---
    -> “I did, just a moment ago.”
        Sasha: “I did, just a moment ago.”
        Fabian: Oh really? Wonderful! I was worried you wouldn’t be able to see him at all, that’s a relief.
        Fabian: So, how was it talking to him again?
        -> “He was distant.”
            Sasha: “He was distant.”
        	He seems genuinely surprised.
        	Fabian: Really? I… Well…
        	He trails off into silence. He wasn’t prepared for this.
	        His voice is equal parts confusion and pity.
	        Fabian: I’m really sorry Sasha.
	        Fabian: He’ll come around. I’m sure he just needs a bit of time.
	        << if $FabianMood gte 1 >>
	        	<< set $FabianMood -= 1 >>
	        << elseif $FabianMood lte -1 >>
	        	<< set $FabianMood += 1 >>
	        << endif >>
        -> “Same as I remembered him.”
            Sasha: “Same as I remembered him.”
	        Fabian: So he’s always been the same jolly chum I see!
	        There is no sarcasm in his voice, but you can tell he’s not being fully serious. You would hardly have called your brother ‘jolly’ in the past.
	        You weren’t honest either, but you have your reasons. There is no need to share everything with him.
	        Fabian: He’s a bit of a closed book sometimes, but I knew he’d cheer up when seeing his lost sibling again.
	        He’s filling in details into your response that were not present. You decide not to correct him.
            << set $FabianMood += 1 >>
        -> “None of your business.”
            Sasha: “None of your business.”
		    Fabian: Alright, no need to be so harsh about it.
		    Fabian: If you’d rather keep this to yourself, I understand.
            Fabian seems disappointed. Either by your tone, or by not hearing about how your meeting with Dmitriy went.
            << set $FabianMood -= 1 >>
    ->  “I don’t want to talk about it.”
        Sasha: “I don’t want to talk about it.”
        Fabian: Oh, alright. I hope that isn’t a bad sign
        Fabian: If you haven’t found him yet, we can go look for him together later, after the parade.
    << set $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Face = true >>
    << jump FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1 >>
-> “When does the Parade start?” << if $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Ashes == true && $FirstLoopFabianParadeTree1Face == true >>
    Sasha: “When does the Parade start?”
    Fabian looks around, scouting the parade grounds for information before replying
    Fabian: I think it will still be a few hours. Most of the other participants of the parade still have to arrive too.
    Fabian: Babushka still needs to come from the River district, and she’ll need help to carry her urn here.
    Fabian: If you wish, you can find a good seat already and wait for the parade to begin.
    You don’t really have much more to do now before the parade, and you have some thoughts to mull over.
    This might be the time to sit down and wait for the parade to start.
    -> “Sure. I’ll just wait until the parade”
        Sasha: “Sure. I’ll just wait until the parade”
        Fabian: Wonderful! I really hope you enjoy it. 
        Fabian: Now if you excuse me, I need to go find someone to help Babushka as I said...
        << Loop >>
		

===
